From: Usama Arif <usamaarif642@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] mm: stop skipping CMA pages in reclaim isolation

Adapt the page-based paths of upstream bfe0857c20c6, which reverts
"mm: skip CMA pages when they are not available" and its MGLRU equivalent.
Skipping consecutive CMA pages without advancing the eligible scan count
can hold the classic LRU lock for a long scan. MGLRU additionally promotes
these pages solely because of their allocation region.

Remove the helper and both uses, retaining the zone filter, mapping and
writeback eligibility checks. This tree uses struct page and sort_page()
rather than the upstream folio API. The other rc5 changes are untouched.
No device speedup or cause of the reported stutters is claimed.

Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/bfe0857c20c663fcc1592fa4e3a61ca12b07dac9
Link: https://lkml.kernel.org/r/9060a32d-b2d7-48c0-8626-1db535653c54@gmail.com
Fixes: 5da226dbfce3 ("mm: skip CMA pages when they are not available")
Signed-off-by: Usama Arif <usamaarif642@gmail.com>
Acked-by: Johannes Weiner <hannes@cmpxchg.org>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -1986,25 +1986,6 @@
 
 }
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_CMA
-/*
- * It is waste of effort to scan and reclaim CMA pages if it is not available
- * for current allocation context. Kswapd can not be enrolled as it can not
- * distinguish this scenario by using sc->gfp_mask = GFP_KERNEL
- */
-static bool skip_cma(struct page *page, struct scan_control *sc)
-{
-	return !current_is_kswapd() &&
-			gfp_migratetype(sc->gfp_mask) != MIGRATE_MOVABLE &&
-			get_pageblock_migratetype(page) == MIGRATE_CMA;
-}
-#else
-static bool skip_cma(struct page *page, struct scan_control *sc)
-{
-	return false;
-}
-#endif
-
 /*
  * Isolating page from the lruvec to fill in @dst list by nr_to_scan times.
  *
@@ -2051,8 +2032,7 @@
 		nr_pages = compound_nr(page);
 		total_scan += nr_pages;
 
-		if (page_zonenum(page) > sc->reclaim_idx ||
-				skip_cma(page, sc)) {
+		if (page_zonenum(page) > sc->reclaim_idx) {
 			nr_skipped[page_zonenum(page)] += nr_pages;
 			move_to = &pages_skipped;
 			goto move;
@@ -4630,7 +4610,7 @@
 	}
 
 	/* ineligible */
-	if (zone > sc->reclaim_idx || skip_cma(page, sc)) {
+	if (zone > sc->reclaim_idx) {
 		gen = page_inc_gen(lruvec, page, false);
 		list_move_tail(&page->lru, &lrugen->lists[gen][type][zone]);
 		return true;
